  "Prodigy M3",
  "Lennox_M3",
  "Prodigy 2.0 BACnet",
  "1404-L4"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Rooftop unit controller BACnet module",
 "applies_to": "Lennox commercial rooftop units that use the Prodigy M3 unit controller.",
 "summary": "The M3 BACnet module plugs onto a Lennox Prodigy M3 rooftop unit controller and exposes it as a BACnet MS/TP device (BTL listed, B-ASC). The BAS drives the unit by writing Analog Outputs (mode, occupancy, setpoints, enables) and reads status from Analog Inputs; occupied/unoccupied setpoints live in Analog Values. The device instance defaults to the MS/TP MAC address. The module expects regular writes from the BAS; if they stop, it times out and falls back to its local control mode.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "Same as MS/TP MAC address",
 "notes": [
  "Default baud 38.4k; Max_Master 127; Max_Info_Frames 1.",
  "Network values should be refreshed at least every 12 minutes (software v7.08+); the communication time-out is 15 minutes (5 minutes before v7.08).",
  "AO101 Application Mode Control takes coded values (heat/cool/fan/exhaust and direct stage commands); see the source for the full code table.",
  "AI200-AI207 (IMC Version characters) are legacy and not recommended for new installations.",
  "AV134-AV140 airflow targets only apply when SmartAirflow is installed; ranges depend on cabinet size.",
  "The module also has Lennox proprietary object types (compressor, blower, heating, economizer, air sensors) with no instance list; they are not included here."
 ],
