 "integration": {
  "summary": "Enable the BACnet module in the M3 setup wizard and set the MAC address, baud and Control Mode. In Room Sensor mode the BMS writes occupancy (AO104) and setpoints (AO109 or AV130-133), and can supply space temperature on AO113. In Network Thermostat mode it sends heat/cool/fan demands on AO101 instead. The M3 does not store commands, so every control point in use must be rewritten on a schedule and after every controller reset.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "AO 104",
    "name": "Occupancy Scheduler Control",
    "why": "0 = occupied, 1-255 = unoccupied; rewrite every 7 min"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 101",
    "name": "Application Mode Control",
    "why": "Mode or direct demand command"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 130",
    "name": "Heating Occupied Setpoint",
    "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, 40-95 °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 131",
    "name": "Cooling Occupied Setpoint",
    "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, 40-95 °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 132",
    "name": "Heating Unoccupied Setpoint",
    "why": "Unoccupied heating setpoint, 40-95 °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 133",
    "name": "Cooling Unoccupied Setpoint",
    "why": "Unoccupied cooling setpoint, 40-95 °F"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 232",
    "name": "Unit Status",
    "why": "HVAC state code: 0 idle, 1 heat, 3 cool, 6 off, 9 fan"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 239",
    "name": "Space Temperature",
    "why": "Space temperature in use"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 253",
    "name": "Current Error",
    "why": "Active alarm code"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "At the M3: SETUP > INSTALL wizard, set Configuration ID 1 position 5 to B to enable the BACnet module. Then SETUP > NETWORK INTEGRATION > BACNET to set the address, baud and CONTROL MODE (Monitor Only, Room Sensor, Network Thermostat, Zone or Remote). In Monitor Only the unit ignores network setpoints and mode demands. No occupancy jumper is needed for Zone/Remote modes.",
  "heartbeat": "Network space temperature (AO113) and space RH/CO2 must be rewritten at least every 5 minutes (2-minute interval recommended), or an alarm is raised; some of these alarms only clear with a local reset. AO101 (network thermostat demand), AO109, AV130-133 and AO104 (when not using setpoint control) must be rewritten within 15 minutes (7-minute interval recommended). Without network sensor data for 5 minutes the unit shows Alarm 73. In Room Sensor mode with BACnet setpoints, 15 minutes with no application-level BACnet traffic makes the RTU reset. In Network Thermostat mode, 15 minutes without demands switches it to its backup mode. After losing network data the unit defaults to occupied (Parameter 225 changes this).",
  "remote_sensors": "Space temperature goes to AO113 (Space Temperature Input) when CONTROL MODE = ROOM SENSOR with network TEMPERATURE = YES. Space RH and CO2 are written to the proprietary space air object properties 536 and 537. Before network sensor data arrives the unit idles up to 5 minutes (Alarm 110), then enters backup sensor mode (Alarm 93). The points list has no network outdoor-air-temperature input.",
  "setup": [
   "Default device instance (Object_Identifier) equals the MS/TP MAC address; change it from the BACnet front end.",
   "Default object name is Lennox_M3_ followed by the MAC address.",
